# What the live-e2e backend serves (see start-backend.sh and the `Live E2E UI`
# job in .github/workflows/ci.yml).
#
# LIVE_BACKEND_APP — the app directory, relative to the repository root, that
#   start-backend.sh boots with this tree's own built `@objectstack/cli`. The
#   live specs target the showcase's objects and seeded records.
#
# There is no published-version pin here any more (objectstack#27154, ruling
#   6464191239 letter D step 2). Until then this file declared
#   OBJECTSTACK_VERSION, the published `@objectstack/*` release the backend
#   ran, and start-backend.sh derived the showcase commit from that release's
#   tag. A HEAD console against a published backend goes red each time the
#   console passes the last release (#25914: 0/5 runs green on 18.1.0 against
#   the 18.2.0 tree), so a required lane on a pin is a lockstep bump on every
#   release. The lane now runs HEAD against HEAD, and the pin, the tag resolve
#   and the npm install retired together.
LIVE_BACKEND_APP=examples/app-showcase
